; error: 7:9: 'add' changes 'xs', the copy this lambda keeps of a slice of the code around it, whose length only the slice itself changes; make the slice inside the lambda, take it as a parameter, 'hold& xs', or keep the slice as a place, '[hold& xs, @s]', in a region declared after it
; The copy a lambda keeps of a slice shares its items, not its length.
task main()
    region r
    flex xs = new [int]() at r
    flex f = [flex @r]() -> int
        xs.add(1)
        <- xs.len
    fi
    show(f())
fi
